    "description": "Circle Power Renewables is a U.S. renewable energy development platform focused on solar, wind and battery-storage projects, principally in Michigan and other regional power markets. Amber Infrastructure and the principals of Circle Power launched the platform in May 2021 after an earlier joint venture; Hunt's 2024 sustainability report identifies Circle Power Renewables as majority Amber-owned, and Amber's current energy-investment materials continue to list the platform as a U.S. investment. Utilities and wholesale power counterparties are its primary end markets. The platform develops projects through dedicated project companies rather than counting each underlying project as a separate manager-level portfolio company: Groveland Mine Solar is owned by Copper Country Power I LLC, a wholly owned Circle Power subsidiary, while 7 Mile Pit Solar is held through a Circle Power project company. Scotia Wind was an early wind-development project of the platform and is therefore not counted as a separate manager-level company.",
